Map dma-buf blobs directly when blobs use fixed mapping.

With fixed blob mapping, each blob is mapped into the prepared shared memory
region with MAP_FIXED, which cannot take the Vulkan import path
(VmMemorySource::Vulkan). Resources with Vulkan info, such as the cross-domain
buffers the Vulkano gralloc allocates, took that path even when their handle
is a dma-buf, so the guest could not map them (screenshots failed in Venus
mode on Apple Silicon). Map such a dma-buf itself instead. Only virglrenderer
(Venus) keeps fixed blob mapping with Vulkano built in
(PATCH.crosvm-fixed-blob-mapping-virglrenderer.patch).

